1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,350
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,350 --> 00:00:04,920
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:04,920 --> 00:00:06,070
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,660 --> 00:00:08,890
I've been a roofer for
forty-two years.

5
00:00:08,930 --> 00:00:10,040
Kneeling on shingles,

6
00:00:10,040 --> 00:00:11,830
crouched on steep pitches,

7
00:00:11,830 --> 00:00:13,310
carrying bundles up a
ladder

8
00:00:13,310 --> 00:00:14,320
on my shoulder.

9
00:00:14,480 --> 00:00:15,530
I had my right knee

10
00:00:15,530 --> 00:00:17,080
replaced two years ago.

11
00:00:17,430 --> 00:00:19,470
It has hurt every day
since.

12
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:21,050
Not surgery pain.

13
00:00:21,130 --> 00:00:22,690
I know what that felt
like,

14
00:00:22,690 --> 00:00:23,750
and it went away.

15
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:25,500
This is different.

16
00:00:25,540 --> 00:00:26,010
Tight.

17
00:00:26,050 --> 00:00:26,690
Full.

18
00:00:26,730 --> 00:00:28,940
Like somebody cinched a
ratchet strap around

19
00:00:28,940 --> 00:00:31,110
the joint and never let it
off.

20
00:00:31,310 --> 00:00:32,570
And for two years

21
00:00:32,570 --> 00:00:34,090
I've been told the same
thing.

22
00:00:34,450 --> 00:00:35,760
Give it time.

23
00:00:35,930 --> 00:00:38,170
At six weeks it was
swelling,

24
00:00:38,170 --> 00:00:39,600
and swelling is normal.

25
00:00:39,780 --> 00:00:41,020
At three months,

26
00:00:41,020 --> 00:00:42,140
give it six.

27
00:00:42,180 --> 00:00:42,950
At six months,

28
00:00:42,950 --> 00:00:44,890
some knees take a full
year.

29
00:00:44,930 --> 00:00:45,470
At a year,

30
00:00:45,470 --> 00:00:47,360
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

31
00:00:47,670 --> 00:00:48,870
And I didn't just wait.

32
00:00:48,930 --> 00:00:50,210
We went down the list.

33
00:00:50,250 --> 00:00:51,700
More physical therapy.

34
00:00:51,930 --> 00:00:52,980
Every session,

35
00:00:52,980 --> 00:00:54,650
every exercise at home,

36
00:00:54,650 --> 00:00:55,870
the same way I never
missed

37
00:00:55,870 --> 00:00:56,950
a day on a job.

38
00:00:57,200 --> 00:00:58,360
I got stronger.

39
00:00:58,400 --> 00:00:59,940
The tightness never moved.

40
00:01:00,040 --> 00:01:01,450
The pain pills helped,

41
00:01:01,450 --> 00:01:02,650
and that was the problem.

42
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:04,500
I'm already on enough
every morning,

43
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:05,250
nobody could tell me

44
00:01:05,250 --> 00:01:06,670
when I'd get to stop,

45
00:01:06,670 --> 00:01:07,350
and you can't be

46
00:01:07,350 --> 00:01:08,500
on a roof foggy.

47
00:01:08,970 --> 00:01:10,270
Then a nerve block.

48
00:01:10,310 --> 00:01:12,130
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

49
00:01:12,330 --> 00:01:13,540
And after that, a second

50
00:01:13,540 --> 00:01:14,670
operation to go back

51
00:01:14,670 --> 00:01:15,730
in and do it over.

52
00:01:16,060 --> 00:01:17,300
I said no.

53
00:01:17,340 --> 00:01:18,890
Every morning I climbed
out

54
00:01:18,890 --> 00:01:20,340
of the truck and my knee
felt

55
00:01:20,340 --> 00:01:22,840
like that strap was
cinched around it,

56
00:01:22,840 --> 00:01:25,370
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

57
00:01:25,690 --> 00:01:27,140
Every morning I took
something

58
00:01:27,140 --> 00:01:28,070
for it and went up

59
00:01:28,070 --> 00:01:29,200
the ladder anyway.

60
00:01:29,420 --> 00:01:30,660
Couldn't kneel on the deck

61
00:01:30,660 --> 00:01:31,980
more than a few minutes,

62
00:01:31,980 --> 00:01:33,740
couldn't stand back up on
a slope

63
00:01:33,740 --> 00:01:35,370
without grabbing for
something,

64
00:01:35,370 --> 00:01:37,330
couldn't carry a bundle up
the ladder,

65
00:01:37,330 --> 00:01:38,760
so I let the young guys do

66
00:01:38,760 --> 00:01:40,750
it and called it
supervising.

67
00:01:40,990 --> 00:01:42,730
By two in the afternoon,

68
00:01:42,730 --> 00:01:43,760
up on a hot roof

69
00:01:43,760 --> 00:01:45,090
with my knee locked,

70
00:01:45,090 --> 00:01:46,010
all I could think about

71
00:01:46,010 --> 00:01:47,080
was getting down.

72
00:01:47,540 --> 00:01:48,790
It woke me at night,

73
00:01:48,790 --> 00:01:50,630
and it turned ordinary
things,

74
00:01:50,630 --> 00:01:51,850
like getting in the truck

75
00:01:51,850 --> 00:01:53,410
or up off the couch,

76
00:01:53,410 --> 00:01:54,530
into a decision.

77
00:01:54,800 --> 00:01:55,900
I'd been doing this since

78
00:01:55,900 --> 00:01:56,980
I was nineteen.

79
00:01:57,300 --> 00:01:58,580
I didn't want my knee to
be

80
00:01:58,580 --> 00:02:00,520
the one that decided when
I quit.

81
00:02:00,750 --> 00:02:02,240
After a long and serious

82
00:02:02,240 --> 00:02:03,580
talk with my wife,

83
00:02:03,580 --> 00:02:05,650
I went back in one more
time.

84
00:02:05,940 --> 00:02:07,200
That was the fourth set

85
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:08,780
of X-rays on this knee.

86
00:02:08,930 --> 00:02:10,560
And like the three before
it,

87
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:13,000
the answer was everything
looks great.

88
00:02:13,040 --> 00:02:15,180
No loosening, no
infection,

89
00:02:15,180 --> 00:02:16,200
nothing wrong.

90
00:02:16,490 --> 00:02:17,680
Only this time

91
00:02:17,680 --> 00:02:19,170
there was no new number.

92
00:02:19,360 --> 00:02:20,440
Nobody said

93
00:02:20,440 --> 00:02:21,760
give it another six
months.

94
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:23,500
There was nothing left to
give it.

95
00:02:23,830 --> 00:02:25,110
I sat in my truck

96
00:02:25,110 --> 00:02:26,880
in the parking lot for a
while.

97
00:02:27,090 --> 00:02:28,500
Okay, I thought.

98
00:02:28,880 --> 00:02:30,200
Then explain this.

99
00:02:30,490 --> 00:02:32,610
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

100
00:02:32,610 --> 00:02:34,080
I hit my breaking point.

101
00:02:34,410 --> 00:02:36,480
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

102
00:02:36,670 --> 00:02:39,700
I had a tear-off starting
at seven,

103
00:02:39,700 --> 00:02:41,860
everyone in the house was
asleep,

104
00:02:41,860 --> 00:02:44,010
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

105
00:02:44,010 --> 00:02:45,120
with my leg up,

106
00:02:45,120 --> 00:02:46,780
trying to find any angle

107
00:02:46,780 --> 00:02:48,490
where it didn't feel like
something

108
00:02:48,490 --> 00:02:51,000
was strapped around my
knee and tightening.

109
00:02:51,260 --> 00:02:53,590
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

110
00:02:53,660 --> 00:02:55,180
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

111
00:02:55,410 --> 00:02:56,320
And I just thought,

112
00:02:56,320 --> 00:02:58,010
is this really my life
now?

113
00:02:58,100 --> 00:02:59,570
I can't live like this.

114
00:02:59,670 --> 00:03:01,420
So I made myself a
promise.

115
00:03:01,540 --> 00:03:02,460
I wouldn't go a day

116
00:03:02,460 --> 00:03:04,060
without looking for an
answer.

117
00:03:04,170 --> 00:03:05,180
And when I found one,

118
00:03:05,180 --> 00:03:06,480
I'd share it with everyone

119
00:03:06,480 --> 00:03:07,790
going through the same
thing.

120
00:03:07,990 --> 00:03:08,980
So I got my laptop

121
00:03:08,980 --> 00:03:10,310
out and went looking.

122
00:03:10,350 --> 00:03:11,470
Not for a product.

123
00:03:11,540 --> 00:03:12,630
For an explanation.

124
00:03:13,010 --> 00:03:14,910
Mayo Clinic forums,

125
00:03:14,910 --> 00:03:17,200
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

126
00:03:17,200 --> 00:03:19,660
doctor videos, medical
animations.

127
00:03:19,820 --> 00:03:21,140
And that's when I found a
video

128
00:03:21,140 --> 00:03:23,010
from a physical therapist
named Dr.

129
00:03:23,050 --> 00:03:24,470
Steven Salinger,

130
00:03:24,470 --> 00:03:25,660
whose own wife had been

131
00:03:25,660 --> 00:03:27,260
through exactly this.

132
00:03:27,540 --> 00:03:29,720
But before I say anything
else,

133
00:03:29,720 --> 00:03:31,030
I want to be straight with
you.

134
00:03:31,070 --> 00:03:33,120
You've already had
something work fast.

135
00:03:33,240 --> 00:03:34,880
The ice pack on the
tailgate.

136
00:03:34,950 --> 00:03:36,490
The first week of a new
pill.

137
00:03:36,700 --> 00:03:38,410
The good day after a
session.

138
00:03:38,530 --> 00:03:39,790
Then it wore off.

139
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:42,020
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

140
00:03:42,200 --> 00:03:44,050
Fast relief isn't relief.

141
00:03:44,090 --> 00:03:45,110
It's a preview.

142
00:03:45,260 --> 00:03:46,350
So I'm not going to tell

143
00:03:46,350 --> 00:03:47,950
you this works fast.

144
00:03:47,990 --> 00:03:48,890
It doesn't.

145
00:03:49,130 --> 00:03:50,960
But if you're willing to
be patient,

146
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:52,110
and to look at what's
going

147
00:03:52,110 --> 00:03:53,500
on around your new knee

148
00:03:53,500 --> 00:03:55,050
instead of inside it,
there

149
00:03:55,050 --> 00:03:57,140
is a real reason it still
hurts.

150
00:03:57,210 --> 00:03:58,910
And something you can do
about it.

151
00:03:59,170 --> 00:04:00,450
Let me explain what he
said,

152
00:04:00,450 --> 00:04:01,690
because this is what
changed

153
00:04:01,690 --> 00:04:02,830
everything for me.

154
00:04:03,020 --> 00:04:04,700
He started with the
basics.

155
00:04:04,930 --> 00:04:06,360
A knee replacement takes
out

156
00:04:06,360 --> 00:04:07,990
the worn joint surfaces
and puts

157
00:04:07,990 --> 00:04:09,350
in metal and plastic.

158
00:04:09,510 --> 00:04:11,350
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

159
00:04:11,350 --> 00:04:13,160
you had before the
operation.

160
00:04:13,420 --> 00:04:14,900
That part I already knew.

161
00:04:15,320 --> 00:04:16,670
But then he explained
something

162
00:04:16,670 --> 00:04:18,170
nobody had ever told me.

163
00:04:18,270 --> 00:04:19,130
He said,

164
00:04:19,130 --> 00:04:20,470
think about a swollen foot

165
00:04:20,470 --> 00:04:21,740
inside a work boot.

166
00:04:21,940 --> 00:04:23,410
The boot didn't shrink.

167
00:04:23,660 --> 00:04:24,640
Your foot

168
00:04:24,640 --> 00:04:26,340
is taking up more room,

169
00:04:26,340 --> 00:04:28,200
so everything feels
cramped

170
00:04:28,200 --> 00:04:29,970
and tight and squeezed.

171
00:04:30,270 --> 00:04:31,360
Your new knee

172
00:04:31,360 --> 00:04:33,440
sits in a limited space
with living

173
00:04:33,440 --> 00:04:35,330
tissue packed all around
it.

174
00:04:35,650 --> 00:04:37,540
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

175
00:04:37,540 --> 00:04:39,150
had to work through that
tissue.

176
00:04:39,440 --> 00:04:42,570
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

177
00:04:42,790 --> 00:04:44,200
At first that's normal.

178
00:04:44,540 --> 00:04:46,250
But in some people that
swelling can

179
00:04:46,250 --> 00:04:48,940
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

180
00:04:49,120 --> 00:04:50,990
And swollen tissue takes
up more

181
00:04:50,990 --> 00:04:52,940
room than calm tissue
does.

182
00:04:53,100 --> 00:04:55,160
So when you bend,

183
00:04:55,160 --> 00:04:56,960
that tissue gets
compressed.

184
00:04:57,140 --> 00:04:58,490
When you straighten,

185
00:04:58,490 --> 00:04:59,910
it gets pulled tight.

186
00:05:00,240 --> 00:05:01,190
That's the strap.

187
00:05:01,230 --> 00:05:03,190
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

188
00:05:03,230 --> 00:05:04,490
And you start being the
one

189
00:05:04,490 --> 00:05:06,400
who stays on the ground
and says,

190
00:05:06,400 --> 00:05:07,290
you guys go ahead.

191
00:05:07,330 --> 00:05:08,490
I'll stay down here.

192
00:05:08,630 --> 00:05:10,120
And that's exactly why so
much

193
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:12,200
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

194
00:05:12,640 --> 00:05:14,410
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

195
00:05:14,410 --> 00:05:15,340
around the knee.

196
00:05:15,440 --> 00:05:16,320
Worth doing,

197
00:05:16,320 --> 00:05:17,310
and I'd done it.

198
00:05:17,420 --> 00:05:18,970
It does nothing about
tissue

199
00:05:18,970 --> 00:05:20,070
taking up room.

200
00:05:20,180 --> 00:05:21,370
A nerve block quiets

201
00:05:21,370 --> 00:05:22,950
the nerve carrying the
signal.

202
00:05:23,280 --> 00:05:25,140
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

203
00:05:25,650 --> 00:05:27,200
But when that irritated
tissue

204
00:05:27,200 --> 00:05:28,730
finally calms down,

205
00:05:28,730 --> 00:05:29,990
it holds less fluid,

206
00:05:29,990 --> 00:05:31,760
and it takes up less room.

207
00:05:32,230 --> 00:05:33,710
Less room taken up means

208
00:05:33,710 --> 00:05:35,570
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

209
00:05:35,610 --> 00:05:37,240
That's what takes the
pressure off.

210
00:05:37,630 --> 00:05:39,130
After two years of this,

211
00:05:39,130 --> 00:05:40,740
it finally made sense.

212
00:05:41,090 --> 00:05:43,110
The problem was never the
new knee.

213
00:05:43,310 --> 00:05:45,170
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

214
00:05:45,350 --> 00:05:46,980
He calls it the squeeze.

215
00:05:47,040 --> 00:05:49,400
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

216
00:05:49,650 --> 00:05:51,230
I'd bought gel kneepads,

217
00:05:51,230 --> 00:05:54,390
knee sleeves, compression
braces, creams,

218
00:05:54,390 --> 00:05:56,110
half of Amazon really,

219
00:05:56,110 --> 00:05:57,310
and all any of it gave

220
00:05:57,310 --> 00:05:58,330
me was an hour.

221
00:05:58,770 --> 00:05:59,770
I even looked at going

222
00:05:59,770 --> 00:06:01,600
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

223
00:06:01,660 --> 00:06:04,000
But at $200 a session

224
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:05,890
with nothing covered by
insurance,

225
00:06:05,890 --> 00:06:07,220
that was a quick no.

226
00:06:07,260 --> 00:06:08,670
Then one night I went

227
00:06:08,670 --> 00:06:09,950
back to that knee
replacement

228
00:06:09,950 --> 00:06:11,260
group and actually read
it.

229
00:06:11,560 --> 00:06:12,960
Thousands of people,

230
00:06:12,960 --> 00:06:14,270
years out from surgery,

231
00:06:14,270 --> 00:06:16,650
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

232
00:06:16,650 --> 00:06:18,060
nobody could explain.

233
00:06:18,150 --> 00:06:19,850
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

234
00:06:19,850 --> 00:06:21,840
the same thing kept coming
up.

235
00:06:22,190 --> 00:06:23,850
This one device,

236
00:06:23,850 --> 00:06:26,070
and people saying it was
the first

237
00:06:26,070 --> 00:06:27,850
thing that made a
difference.

238
00:06:27,890 --> 00:06:29,740
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

239
00:06:29,740 --> 00:06:30,990
alright, here it comes,

240
00:06:30,990 --> 00:06:32,490
he's selling me something,

241
00:06:32,490 --> 00:06:34,230
let me shut that down
right now.

242
00:06:34,500 --> 00:06:35,880
I'm only here because I
made

243
00:06:35,880 --> 00:06:37,360
myself a promise at 2:30

244
00:06:37,360 --> 00:06:38,170
in the morning that if I

245
00:06:38,170 --> 00:06:39,940
ever found something that
helped,

246
00:06:39,940 --> 00:06:41,020
I'd say so.

247
00:06:41,300 --> 00:06:42,740
It's called the KenRelief
Red

248
00:06:42,740 --> 00:06:44,060
Light Therapy Wrap.

249
00:06:44,240 --> 00:06:46,420
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

250
00:06:46,670 --> 00:06:48,820
It looked like the cheap
knee sleeves

251
00:06:48,820 --> 00:06:51,030
off Amazon that did
nothing for me.

252
00:06:51,380 --> 00:06:53,370
But I went to their
website anyway,

253
00:06:53,370 --> 00:06:54,600
just to see what all

254
00:06:54,600 --> 00:06:55,810
the fuss was about.

255
00:06:56,170 --> 00:06:58,780
It's the same red light
therapy clinics

256
00:06:58,780 --> 00:07:01,160
charge $200 a session

257
00:07:01,160 --> 00:07:02,760
for, off machines that
cost

258
00:07:02,760 --> 00:07:04,360
fifty thousand dollars,

259
00:07:04,360 --> 00:07:05,430
in a wrap you plug

260
00:07:05,430 --> 00:07:06,730
into the wall at home.

261
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,670
Two hundred and forty
lights.

262
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:11,010
Red at 660 nanometers

263
00:07:11,010 --> 00:07:13,460
and near-infrared at 850,

264
00:07:13,460 --> 00:07:15,660
run together for the
strongest effect.

265
00:07:16,010 --> 00:07:17,390
Four strength levels.

266
00:07:17,430 --> 00:07:19,240
A five to thirty minute
timer.

267
00:07:19,300 --> 00:07:20,780
Then I saw the guarantee.

268
00:07:20,820 --> 00:07:21,960
Ninety days.

269
00:07:22,120 --> 00:07:24,000
Results or your money
back,

270
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:25,450
no questions,

271
00:07:25,450 --> 00:07:26,810
no store credit,

272
00:07:26,810 --> 00:07:28,510
and you don't even send it
back.

273
00:07:28,610 --> 00:07:30,210
I put a warranty on every

274
00:07:30,210 --> 00:07:31,540
roof I've ever done,

275
00:07:31,540 --> 00:07:32,730
and nobody ever gave me

276
00:07:32,730 --> 00:07:33,780
one on my knee.

277
00:07:33,870 --> 00:07:35,250
There wasn't much to lose,

278
00:07:35,250 --> 00:07:36,240
so I ordered it.

279
00:07:36,500 --> 00:07:37,740
Two of them, actually.

280
00:07:37,930 --> 00:07:39,970
Only the right knee was
replaced,

281
00:07:39,970 --> 00:07:42,180
but you favor the leg that
